  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The Akkadian, Ugaritic and Aramaic head nouns support a sense broad enough for poetic uses alongside רֹאשׁ. Whether the verb for bowing derives from the head noun is uncertain. Targum Onkelos renders the spice in Exodus 30:24 with its word for cassia (Jastrow S01818). The text gives its weight and use but leaves the plant species and the origin of its name open."
